{"candidates":[{"content":"Expose the suspension boundary as a first-class diagnostic artifact: for each UNDECIDED node, record its full attacker set and the maximal defense chains that failed to reinstate it. This is a pure read-only projection of the final labeling, so determinism of the fixed point, polynomial cost, reinstatement-as-derived, and validity of every committed root are untouched. The strengthening is operational: the boundary atlas, with per-node witness chains, becomes admissible evidence for the next conjecture iteration, so subsequent warrants can attack the symmetry that produced the suspension instead of re-litigating settled nodes. This directly targets the spec's own diagnosis that the whole question lives in edge construction, not in the label computation.","evidence_refs":[{"block":"0c302d11d621778b","quote":"The grounded extension itself was never the problem"},{"block":"0e806619395ec8f4","quote":"**Labels are a pure function of the graph.**"},{"block":"0909868ae3d22218"}],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"src-8ddb400f3c2d52a681266c7cebc3b1898bac6750"}],"typicality":0.82},{"content":"Compute a fragility profile for every accepted (IN) node by single-edge deletion: for each attack edge e targeting or defending the node, run the fixpoint on the graph minus e and record whether the node's label flips. Nodes invariant to every single-edge deletion are 'robust'; nodes that flip are 'fragile'. This is deterministic and polynomial — O(|E|) fixpoint runs, each linear — and read-only, so all four guarantees are preserved. The skeptical semantics hides that acceptance is a spectrum: a node can be IN while resting on exactly one attack edge whose removal flips it. Fragile accepted nodes become priority targets for additional defense warrants, strengthening the extension without altering its label function.","evidence_refs":[{"block":"0e806619395ec8f4","quote":"**Labels are a pure function of the graph.**"},{"block":"1dd041117ca8c54a","quote":"Nothing in this system is refuted by being disliked."}],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"src-8ddb400f3c2d52a681266c7cebc3b1898bac6750"}],"typicality":0.72},{"content":"Make edge construction itself a second least fixpoint: formalize warrant-carriage → attack-edge materialization (including the closure rule) as a monotone operator on the finite edge lattice, and compute its least fixpoint before Pass 1. The composition of two least fixpoints on finite lattices is deterministic and polynomial; reinstatement remains a derived property inside Pass 1; committed roots stay valid provided the edge operator is root-preserving — it only materializes edges already carried by registered warrants and never invents acceptance. This moves the skeptical guarantees down to the place the spec names as the real locus of the question, making edge provenance auditable as a fixpoint in its own right and exposing where monotonicity could silently break.","evidence_refs":[{"block":"0c302d11d621778b","quote":"The grounded extension itself was never the problem"},{"block":"0a6dd2576c1bf4cb"}],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"src-8ddb400f3c2d52a681266c7cebc3b1898bac6750"}],"typicality":0.55},{"content":"Counterexample to the most tempting expansion: resolving suspensions by bounded-depth lookahead and promoting UNDECIDED nodes. In the grounded extension a node is IN iff all its attackers are eventually OUT, so every UNDECIDED node has at least one attacker that is not OUT in the final labeling. Any promotion of such a node either adds nothing (all-attackers-OUT nodes are already IN) or changes the acceptance rule and can create conflict cycles — a promoted node whose attacker is also promoted — breaking determinism of the fixed point and reinstatement-as-derived. Negative result: the lever is the edge set, not the labeling rule; naive 'reinstatement acceleration' is a trap that must be refused.","evidence_refs":[{"block":"09ffabcd92979168","quote":"# Pass 1: attack (Dung grounded extension; unique, skeptical, polynomial)"},{"block":"0c302d11d621778b","quote":"The grounded extension itself was never the problem"}],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"src-8ddb400f3c2d52a681266c7cebc3b1898bac6750"}],"typicality":0.25},{"content":"Close the loop from suspension to edge synthesis: when the boundary atlas shows a stable suspension pattern across two genuinely different school families, auto-register a probe warrant that attacks the suspended cluster from an exogenous anchor — the LAMBDA_FLOOR role the spec calls load-bearing, not decorative. Because the new edge is a registered warrant with normal carriage rules, it faces the same scrutiny and can itself be attacked; per-run determinism and polynomial cost are preserved because the fixpoint runs on the new edge set exactly as before, and committed-root validity holds since new edges only ever attack, never invent acceptance. Counterexample: auto-generated warrants can be spurious, so synthesis must be gated on cross-family stability and the generated warrant must carry provenance back to the atlas that triggered it.","evidence_refs":[{"block":"1e2811a698f6d3f3","quote":"**Brake 1 — HV floor as criterion, never as gate.**"},{"block":"1b2d5ddadda17971"}],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"src-8ddb400f3c2d52a681266c7cebc3b1898bac6750"}],"typicality":0.3},{"content":"Extend the closure rule along the warrant's support chain: an attack on any support node at depth d inherits as an attack on the warrant's target, but only if the chain is broken at that point (all intermediate nodes attacked or absent), capped at depth D. Enforce entirely in att construction, label-free, so the edge operator stays monotone and the fixpoint's kind is unchanged. Polynomial via the depth cap; deterministic as a pure function of the graph; reinstatement remains derived inside Pass 1. This makes support-chain fragility visible to the extension — a warrant whose evidence chain is undermined anywhere becomes attackable — while preserving committed-root validity because inheritance only ever adds attacks, never acceptance. The trap: inheritance can create self-attack cycles; prove acyclicity via provenance ordering plus the depth cap.","evidence_refs":[{"block":"0974daebd1665965","quote":"- **Closure rule:** any attacker of `validity_node` attacks the warrant (hence its carrier's attack edge)."},{"block":"1dd041117ca8c54a","quote":"Nothing in this system is refuted by being disliked."}],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"src-8ddb400f3c2d52a681266c7cebc3b1898bac6750"}],"typicality":0.45}],"simulation_proposals":[]}